   "date": "2019-01-23T20:22:49Z",
   "subject": "Daily log in GGIR",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\" lang=\"EN-GB\">Hi Vincent and all GGIR users,</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\" lang=\"EN-GB\">Firstly, thank you for amazing work. I am responsible for accelerometer-data\r\nprocessing at our department.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\" lang=\"EN-GB\"><br></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\" lang=\"EN-GB\">We use regularly about 400 ActiGraphs and 70 Axivity. I went over some issues\r\nwith GGIR regarding to date-format, character used to separate decimals etc (mostly based on eastern Europe <br></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\" lang=\"EN-GB\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;line-height:107%;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\" lang=\"EN-GB\">settings</span> of windows).\r\nNow, I am using it with no errors at all, and I&#39;m very happy with that. I just\r\nwould like to ask three questions: <br>\r\n<br>\r\n</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\" lang=\"EN-GB\">\r\n1. Is there (or will be soon) any chance to use &quot;daily log&quot; with\r\ntimetable to separate outcomes of physical activity for specific time-period (e.g.\r\nbefore-school, in-school, after-school, during PE lessons...)?<br>\r\n<br>\r\n</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\" lang=\"EN-GB\">2. Is there any way to translate labels into Czech language in participant&#39;s\r\nfeedback? We would like to provide it to children and not all of them are good\r\nin English.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\" lang=\"EN-GB\"> </span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\" lang=\"EN-GB\">3. Is there in GGIR community an agreement of mg threshold for\r\nclassifying moderate physical activity among children (for ActiGraph,\r\nnon-dominant wrist)? It is 201.4 mg based on Hildebrand et al. 2014? For Czech\r\nchildren, it seems to be to high :D.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\" lang=\"EN-GB\"><br>\r\nNote: I am a complete beginner in R, the GGIR was a reason why I recently\r\ninstalled it.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\" lang=\"EN-GB\"> </span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\" lang=\"EN-GB\">Thank you.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\" lang=\"EN-GB\"> </span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\" lang=\"EN-GB\">Jan Dygryn,</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\" lang=\"EN-GB\">Institute of Active Lifestyle</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\" lang=\"EN-GB\">Palacký University Olomouc, Czech Republic.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<br><span><span title=\"\"></span></span></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "lHbCePF2AwAJ",
   "from": "Vincent van Hees",
   "author": "8d92e34685fbc6bd",
