   "subject": "Re: [GGIR] Daily log in GGIR",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Thank you Jan,</div><div>Glad to hear you managed to get GGIR to work.</div><div>The decimal separator of the machine is indeed something that needs looking into, <a href=\"https://github.com/wadpac/GGIR/issues/116\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/wadpac/GGIR/issues/116&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792491278492000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0unJWSAGtJKmG-kv3sUvw-\">we are aware of it</a>.</div><div><br></div><div dir=\"ltr\">1. This is possible with argument qwindow (see package documentation for details).<div>2. Sorry not at the moment. However, it would be possible to develop this as an extra functionality where you as user specify the text that needs to be in the pdf reports. Either hire me to do it (<a href=\"https://www.movementdata.nl/how-to-help-sustain-ggir\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.movementdata.nl/how-to-help-sustain-ggir&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792491278492000&amp;usg=AOvVaw325L1-jiWbpF6GfgbWxLUT\">https://www.movementdata.nl/how-to-help-sustain-ggir</a>) or find someone else to build this.</div><div>3. You may want to read the papers by Lynne Boddy, Alex Rowlands, and/or Stuart Fairclough as well.</div><div><br></div><div>Best, Vincent</div></div></div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_attr\">On Wed, 23 Jan 2019 at 21:22, Jan &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">jan.d...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:<br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\" lang=\"EN-GB\">Hi Vincent and all GGIR users,</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\" lang=\"EN-GB\">Firstly, thank you for amazing work. I am responsible for accelerometer-data\r\nprocessing at our department.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\" lang=\"EN-GB\"><br></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\" lang=\"EN-GB\">We use regularly about 400 ActiGraphs and 70 Axivity. I went over some issues\r\nwith GGIR regarding to date-format, character used to separate decimals etc (mostly based on eastern Europe <br></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\" lang=\"EN-GB\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;line-height:107%;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\" lang=\"EN-GB\">settings</span> of windows).\r\nNow, I am using it with no errors at all, and I&#39;m very happy with that. I just\r\nwould like to ask three questions: <br>\r\n<br>\r\n</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\" lang=\"EN-GB\">\r\n1. Is there (or will be soon) any chance to use &quot;daily log&quot; with\r\ntimetable to separate outcomes of physical activity for specific time-period (e.g.\r\nbefore-school, in-school, after-school, during PE lessons...)?<br>\r\n<br>\r\n</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\" lang=\"EN-GB\">2. Is there any way to translate labels into Czech language in participant&#39;s\r\nfeedback? We would like to provide it to children and not all of them are good\r\nin English.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\" lang=\"EN-GB\"> </span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\" lang=\"EN-GB\">3. Is there in GGIR community an agreement of mg threshold for\r\nclassifying moderate physical activity among children (for ActiGraph,\r\nnon-dominant wrist)? It is 201.4 mg based on Hildebrand et al. 2014? For Czech\r\nchildren, it seems to be to high :D.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\" lang=\"EN-GB\"><br>\r\nNote: I am a complete beginner in R, the GGIR was a reason why I recently\r\ninstalled it.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\" lang=\"EN-GB\"> </span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\" lang=\"EN-GB\">Thank you.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\" lang=\"EN-GB\"> </span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\" lang=\"EN-GB\">Jan Dygryn,</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\" lang=\"EN-GB\">Institute of Active Lifestyle</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\" lang=\"EN-GB\">Palacký University Olomouc, Czech Republic.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<br><span><span title=\"\"></span></span></div>\r\n\r\n<p></p></blockquote></div>"
